WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.290
- If you look at certain areas,

00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:06.620
solar panels, solar technology
generally, batteries,

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:10.990
electric vehicle
technology, semiconductors,

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:12.760
other parts of the supply chain,

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:16.910
we have in America over
the past several decades,

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:20.770
just watched our domestic
supply chain vanish

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:21.733
before our eyes.

00:00:21.733 --> 00:00:24.316
(gentle music)

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.260
When president elect Biden called me

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:36.880
to ask me to do the job,

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:41.350
we talked about being domestically focused

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:44.470
and rebuilding from within

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:47.200
which by the way, we think is the best way

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.860
to be competitive globally.

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:53.437
So it's about investing in talent,

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:57.680
investing in research and development,

00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:59.980
making sure that we can compete globally

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:04.980
by having stronger technology
internally in America.

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:07.400
- In the domestic agenda are there areas

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:10.260
where you think, this
would be a great area

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:12.750
that Chinese investment
might work, might help?

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:15.630
- We are at this point experiencing

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:17.300
kind of good collaboration

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.360
with the Chinese as it relates to climate.

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:23.260
So I think that that is an area
where our goals are aligned.

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:24.920
And we know that in order to hit

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:29.923
President Biden's climate change targets,

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:33.290
we're heavily dependent on technology,

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:36.800
the technology necessary
to hit his climate goals

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:37.910
doesn't exist today.

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:41.390
I can't emphasize this enough
on a case-by-case basis.

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:43.440
It depends on who is the investor,

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.700
is there state involvement,
what are their goals?

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:50.017
And we are serious about
protecting our national security.

00:01:50.017 --> 00:01:53.050
- Let me ask you kind of how
you come to your thinking

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:55.540
about international trade
and China in particular,

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:57.890
as I understand that your
father used to work at Bulova,

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:00.550
was laid off with Chinese competition.

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:02.340
You were the governor and
you were the treasurer

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:06.140
at a time when the costume
jewelry industry got clobbered

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:07.360
by Chinese competition.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.290
So how much does that kind of factor

00:02:09.290 --> 00:02:10.850
into the way you think about things?

00:02:10.850 --> 00:02:12.540
- I think, significantly.

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:15.290
That was my personal story,
it was really hard, right?

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:18.670
And Rhode Island, like so
many places in the Midwest,

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:20.370
in the eighties, seventies,

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:23.470
was a vibrant manufacturing economy

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:25.290
and there was a job there for everybody.

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:28.890
And then it all went away in
search of cheap labor to China,

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:31.480
cheap labor drove out manufacturing.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:33.650
So the president is committed

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:37.360
to bringing that back to America, as am I,

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:38.930
it's a big part of my story.

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:42.720
In fact, when I was thinking
about taking the job,

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.370
it was a hard decision
and I called my brother

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:47.760
and I said, "The president
wants me to do this."

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:50.070
And he said, "Gina, dad would be so proud

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:51.360
if you could play a role

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:54.060
in getting manufacturing
going again in America."

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:56.970
So for me, it's a huge motivator.

00:02:56.970 --> 00:03:01.970
- Would you imagine
taking delegations of CEOs

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:05.270
or senior business officials abroad

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:08.110
to look at export or even
investment opportunities?

00:03:08.110 --> 00:03:09.600
Is that something you think you would do?

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:10.600
- Yes, absolutely.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:15.600
A big part of my job is export
promotion and I'm looking,

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:17.130
for example, we're launching

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:20.470
a clean tech export promotion initiative.

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:23.880
We really want to do a better job

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:27.650
helping American businesses
export their clean technology.

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:30.650
Any place that I see market interference

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:34.320
by state actors or other governments

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:36.880
or unfairness or an unlevel playing field

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:39.930
for American companies trying
to access global markets,

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:42.090
that is definitely a huge part of my job

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:45.230
to kind of stick up for American industry.

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:48.400
- Would China be one of the
places you imagine taking,

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.050
you expect to take CEOs?

00:03:50.050 --> 00:03:51.180
- I think so, yes.

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:53.010
Once travel opens,

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:56.150
Asia and China are very important markets.

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:58.300
Obviously a part of my day every day

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:00.860
is talking to American businesses.

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:04.163
The Chinese market is huge and growing.

00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:06.870
And they don't play by the rules,

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:07.703
they're not living up

00:04:07.703 --> 00:04:10.460
to their phase one purchase commitments,

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:13.190
they rip off our intellectual property,

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:17.370
there's all kinds of barriers
that they're putting in place

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:18.920
which prevent American businesses

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:20.810
from accessing that market.

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:24.120
So I plan to be a forceful advocate

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:25.560
on behalf of American business,

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:29.140
and yes, to ramp up our direct engagement

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:33.470
with my counterparts in China
and bring businesses there.

00:04:33.470 --> 00:04:36.640
- So it doesn't sound like you agree

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:39.930
with the idea of the two
economies decoupling.

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:42.820
- Absolutely not. I don't
really think that's an option.

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:46.430
I mean, the size and
scale of their economy

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:50.670
is such that we need access to that market

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:52.490
and they need and want
to access to this market.

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:57.230
So we need robust commercial
engagement with China

00:04:57.230 --> 00:05:01.240
that does not in any way ever compromise

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:02.800
our national security.

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:04.700
- This administration has
talked about cooperation

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:06.240
in some areas like climate,

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:08.750
do you think then in the
trade and economic area,

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:11.040
we're in the cooperation basket

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.290
or the, let's just say,
confrontation basket?

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:15.820
- A little of both.

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:17.649
Cooperation is the goal

00:05:17.649 --> 00:05:21.830
but we can't be taken advantage of, right?

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:24.400
So if they're gonna block our companies,

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:26.180
if they're going to flood our market

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:28.490
with cheap steel and aluminum

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:31.110
which hurts our steel
and aluminum industry,

00:05:31.110 --> 00:05:35.440
if they're going to not respect

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:37.700
protection of intellectual property,

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:40.450
well, then we'll be
confrontational when we need to be.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:45.183
But also we need to do business there,

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:47.280
and that's something

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:50.930
that I think it's just an economic fact,

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:53.570
it's complex, and it is fraught.

00:05:53.570 --> 00:05:56.810
Communication helps. I think
a lot of communication helps.

00:05:56.810 --> 00:06:00.570
I actually think robust
commercial engagement

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:05.570
will help to mitigate
any potential tensions.

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:10.083
If we could continue our
commercial engagement,

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:14.750
it will help prevent unintended conflict

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:16.850
which can come from lack of communication.

